# Keep `docs/what-to-test.md` up to date

`docs/what-to-test.md` is a short manual checklist. After a change a tester
could notice — UI, recipe content, calculations, persistence, migrations,
notifications, routing — add an entry before finishing.

## Rules

- Add new entries at the top, under the `---` separator.
- Never delete or rewrite existing entries. The user clears the file manually.
- One entry per change, not per file touched.
- Skip it for changes with no observable effect: docs, comments, formatting,
  test-only edits.

## Format

```markdown
## <date> — <short title>

- [ ] <what to verify, one short line>
```

## Writing the items

Keep them blunt and few — a handful of lines, not a test plan. Name the thing
to check, not how to check it or why ("Confirm old realizations migrated
correctly", not a paragraph about the migration).

Cover only what could plausibly break. Always include existing stored data when
a migration or payload changed, and the other locale when text changed.
